  "f-size-decides#parallel": {
   "verdict": null,
   "note": "I think if we provide the caveat that 10+ manual has very low n, we can argue there is actually negligible difference. People often say the agent is faster but I'm not sure that's really supported. These bars are pretty close. We can point out that both plan quality and speed to create are very slightly agent-favoured if at al, and that the use of each seems logical. We have a retired finding I think about operators who rely more not being better - a single number or two from there might help.",
   "links": [],
   "tags": [],
   "updated": "2026-10-14T11:18:52.219Z"
